# Ship workflow (changelog, docs, commit)

## Change log ↔ app summary

After **meaningful** work in **`GoDiveMVP/`**, update docs in the **same effort**:

1. **`GoDiveMVP/cursor/change_log.md`** — append unpushed batch: Summary line + bullets.
2. **`GoDiveMVP/cursor/app_summary.md`** — only when architecture or user-visible behavior changes; **surgical** edit (≤2 short sentences per batch); do not mirror every changelog bullet.

**`change_log.md`:** one running batch only; shipped history lives in git. Reset only after successful commit+push you perform (**below**). Do not reset if push failed or user did not request ship.

**`app_summary.md`:** scannable map — not a changelog. Update for new/removed tabs, models, flows, data rules; skip polish, refactors, tests-only.

## GitHub Pages user guide

Before commit/push, sync **`docs/`** (MkDocs) when the batch changes user-visible behavior (screens, workflows, data rules, settings labels). Source: **`app_summary.md`**, **`change_log.md`**, code if stale.

Skip: visual polish, performance, internal refactors, agent rules, test-only changes. No release-note prose on Pages.

Push order: finish app + cursor docs → sync **`docs/`** → Xcode preflight (**`xcode-workflow.mdc`**) → commit → push.

## Commit message shape

Subject (≤72 chars, imperative) + body:

```text
Short subject.

## Summary
One or two sentences.

## Features
- …

## Bug fixes
- …

## Notes (optional)
- Tests, docs, migration
```

Pull bullets from **`change_log.md`**. Synthesize — do not paste entire change log.

## Commit + push steps

1. Ensure **`change_log.md`** / **`app_summary.md`** reflect the work.
2. Sync **`docs/`** when functional user-facing changes ship.
3. iPhone 17 sim preflight per **`xcode-workflow.mdc`** (`build-for-testing` + scoped tests for the batch) — do not commit until green, 0 project warnings.
4. Draft commit body from **`change_log.md`** **before** clearing it.
5. Reset **`change_log.md`** to empty template (header + intro only); stage cleared file in the same commit.
6. **`git commit`** (HEREDOC subject + body) → **`git push`** when requested.

Do not push without preflight. Do not use one-line subject only for multi-item batches.

## Changelog reset template

```markdown
# Change Log

**Since last push** — running notes for the current batch. Cleared after each successful **commit + push**; shipped history lives in **git**.

Agents: append summaries and bullets here during work; refresh **`cursor/app_summary.md`** for architecture.

---

```

Do not reset if not shipping in this task. Do not restore shipped bullets after reset.
